records.methods:
Inclusion criteria for the APT: positive MABSC-PD diagnosis based on American Thoracic Society criteria; any age and sex; no MABSC-PD treatment in 12 months prior; and for OC: ≥1 MABSC positive respiratory culture; any age and sex; no MABSC-PD treatment in 12 months prior. The first interim analysis (IA) in April 2026 will analyse data from 60 APT participants who have completed 6 weeks short intensive therapy (SI) using the Sequential Multiple Assignment Randomised Trial approach, thus providing the first randomised assessment of standard of care treatments. Following IA a new treatment arm using combined B-lactam antimicrobials will be initiated. The APT has 3 nested trials – the first compares efficacy and tolerance at 6 weeks. The primary outcome measures are: MABSC clearance – defined as 3 negative respiratory samples (sputum/induced sputum) or 1 negative bronchoalveolar lavage collected at Week 4; and Treatment tolerance – defined as no adverse events (AEs) or AEs possibly/probably/definitely related to study drugs graded 1 or 2 based on the Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events Version 5.0.

